{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1132283-question-about-the-wild-hunt","id":1132283,"title":"Question About the Wild Hunt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-21T10:39:26-07:00","id":1132283,"title":"Question About the Wild Hunt","content":"For Gods such as Odin, Arawn, Donn, and others who lead the Wild Hunt, how is that particular phenomenon accounted for in Second Edition? Does it fall under a purview? If not, is it part of the hunter calling? Also no offense to the previous version and homebrew solutions but just slapping it into the Animal purview is an inadequate solution as the goal of the hunt is to chase and catch a intelligent and sentient target (such as a soul which escaped the underworld, someone who was an awful person in life, a non-human entity, etc). The animals present are usually horses and hounds which would normally be part of a hunting party, which therefore excludes Animal. Especially if you factor in that traditonally only humans could join the hunt, there being no mention of local wild life being invited to the best of my knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T11:58:02-07:00","id":1132331,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure of the terminology, but maybe the wild hunt is purchased as minions you can summon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T15:36:58-07:00","id":1132414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1132283-question-about-the-wild-hunt#post1132283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Gods such as Odin, Arawn, Donn, and others who lead the Wild Hunt, how is that particular phenomenon accounted for in Second Edition? Does it fall under a purview? If not, is it part of the hunter calling? Also no offense to the previous version and homebrew solutions but just slapping it into the Animal purview is an inadequate solution as the goal of the hunt is to chase and catch a intelligent and sentient target (such as a soul which escaped the underworld, someone who was an awful person in life, a non-human entity, etc). The animals present are usually horses and hounds which would normally be part of a hunting party, which therefore excludes Animal. Especially if you factor in that traditonally only humans could join the hunt, there being no mention of local wild life being invited to the best of my knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to toss this question into the &quot;Ask Neall,&quot; thread Manannansun, that's where most of the answers to people's questions are given with exception to the threads about new bits of released information. I would expect, however, that there is no single way to handle all of the Wild Hunt concepts. While the notion of the concept of the Wild Hunt is centered mainly in north-western Europe, starting in the medieval period, the actual details of exactly what it entails can vary so wildly that the best way to represent it is probably on a unique basis to each individual who leads their culture's representation of the hunt. <br /> <br /> For example, as you mentioned, the Hunt is described as having a wide variety of targets, each with different reasons behind them, each part of a different culture's own primarily medieval worldview. While all of these are collectively dubbed 'The Wild Hunt,' that is a modern term grouping a large series of traditions across considerable space and time. If you spoke to a 15th century English noble and discussed Arthur leading hunts for lost souls, a 10th century Danish jarl about ideas of Odin leading a hunt, 10th century Irish Ri about Sidhe hunts, and a 13th century French serf about the Devil riding across the sky to claim the souls of the damned, I expect none of them would consider their notions similar at all.<br /> <br /> Due to this, I expect each individual figure who is sometimes mentioned as leading a hunt such as this would have this represented mechanically in a different way. Hunting for lost souls for sport? That could be Hunter based off the name, but we don't actually know much about it. Hunting for lost souls to return them to an Afterlife? Could be Liminal, or Death. Hunting a human being for some sort of violation against the will of the Divine? Could be Order. Hunting just to cause problems, for your own joy, but bringing massive problems in your wake? Chaos.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I think that since 'The Wild Hunt,' is a modern term imposed on a thematic concept, sort of like 'Divine King,' or 'Fisher King,' the exact details of this would be culture, if not figure-specific. I don't think Odin, King Arthur, Satan, Archangel Michael, Cernunnos (though this one is a modern reimagining since Cernunnos is a 'problem deity' and was, if he existed as a unified concept at all, more likely a deity of wealth), and other Huntsmasters are all doing the exact same thing. Maybe they are all repeating an archtype, but the details are all sufficiently different I expect they are best represented with different Purviews, Callings, or as Shadryx suggests, simply Followers.<br /> <br /> Oh, and, I think you may be misunderstanding one of the Scion 2.0 houseruled Animal Boons. The Boon, 'Wild Hunt,' is using the name of the concept. It isn't the only way to preform The Wild Hunt in the slightest. The Boon used the name since it is catchy, and memorable for people, tying in a folkloric concept, not that it is the exact way all such hunts are called. Also, our Animal Purview does allow domesticated animals such as horses and hounds too, the Animal Purview has always allowed for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T08:08:44-07:00","id":1144776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1132283-question-about-the-wild-hunt?p=1132331#post1132331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure of the terminology, but maybe the wild hunt is purchased as minions you can summon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having played the Witcher 3 recently, can't help but imagine someone summoning Eredin and his gang from a fanny pack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}